================================================================================
SUMMARY
================================================================================
A SwiftUI + Apple-HIG parity of the web BatteryHealthPage (route /battery), adaptive across macOS + iOS
(ADR-002/006). The page binds an injectable BatteryHealthDataSource seam (loadVehicles/Analytics/
Prediction/Sessions/Live — the web useSelectedVehicle + useBatteryHealthAnalytics + useBatteryDegradation
+ useChargingSessionsPaginated + useChargingTelemetryLatest queries) through the @Observable
BatteryHealthPageModel; the view holds no networking (ADR-004) and every quantity is SI on disk (kWh
capacity as the analytics endpoint serves it, SI kilometres range, SI Celsius module temps, watt-hour
session energy), converted only at the render boundary via the shared Units facade (ADR-005). It
reproduces the web chrome (title + subtitle + header VehicleSelect + LiveIndicator), the health-score
hero (4 gauges + band badge + years-to-80), the 3 metric bars, the 7 summary cards, the thermal panel
(+ ADR-013 freshness chip), the smart-insights grid, the capacity-trend projection (actual + dashed-
projected, 80/70 references), the estimated-range area chart, the charge-level distribution + habit
tiles, the capacity-&-range new-vs-now panel, the AC/DC donut beside the charging-statistics list, the
quick-links grid, and the recommendations panel — all from the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (no
hand-rolled glass, no direct Charts, no WKWebView). The web RadialGauge is reproduced natively as the
shared EnergyGauge (value+unit centre) since TSRadialGauge renders a percentage; the web dual-line
ComposedChart becomes a TSLineChart with the actual->projected bridge preserved. Every data source
implements loading/empty/error/success and every section its own empty state; the 10 web
